{"abstract":"Automatic coreference resolution is understudied in Danish even though most of the Danish Dependency Treebank (Buch-Kromann, 2003) is annotated with coreference relations. This paper describes a conversion of its partial, yet well-documented, coreference relations into coreference clusters and the training and evaluation of coreference models on this data. To the best of our knowledge, these are the first publicly available, neural coreference models for Danish. We also present a new entity linking annotation on the dataset using WikiData identifiers, a named entity disambiguation (NED) dataset, and a larger automatically created NED dataset enabling wikily supervised NED models. The entity linking annotation is benchmarked using a state-of-the-art neural entity disambiguation model.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Barrett, Maria","Lam, Hieu","Wu, Martin","Lacroix, Ophélie","Plank, Barbara","Søgaard, Anders"],"cuid":["S02-088.21-038281"],"event":{"end":"2021-11-11","place":"Punta Cana, Dominican Republic","start":"2021-11-10","title":"4th Workshop on Computational Models of Reference, Anaphora and Coreference","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Coreference Resolution","Coreference clusters","Danish language processing","Dependency Treebank","Entity Linking","Named entity disambiguation NED","Natural Language Processing NLP","Neural models","Wikidata","Wikily supervised models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-ALX"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-ALX","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"resources and evaluations for danish entity resolution","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2021.crac-1.7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-088.21-038281","identifier":[{"id":"85130436151","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-32b31ef4-6f3b-44b1-809b-87bf07069577","ku-13d9a170-9291-48a1-9988-d295445f092a"],"keyword":["Coreference clusters","Coreference resolution","Danish language processing","Dependency Treebank","Entity linking","Named entity disambiguation (NED)","Natural language processing (NLP)","Neural models","WikiData","Wikily supervised models"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-10F530CE718F10D310E07EC036FD5E47"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86421903/2021.crac_1.7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/300081522/Resources_and_Evaluations_for_Danish_Entity_Resolution.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2021.crac-1.7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2021.crac-1.7.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"alexandra institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-ALX","l3nn":"Alexandra Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Alexandra Institute","namevar":["Alexandra Instituttet A/S (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-ALX","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Natural Language Processing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Jung","key":"barrettpau","last":"Barrett","locid":"ffc6db77-95ed-452f-92ac-ca143a9db73c","name":"Barrett, Maria Jung","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hieu","key":"lampau","last":"Lam","name":"Lam, Hieu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Martin","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Martin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ophélie","key":"lacroixpau","last":"Lacroix","name":"Lacroix, Ophélie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Anders","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"5cfea506-104a-4b40-b63b-e29d037159b0","name":"Søgaard, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-5250-4276","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2021.crac-1.7","pages":"63-69","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Fourth Workshop on Computational Models of Reference, Anaphora and Coreference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-32b31ef4-6f3b-44b1-809b-87bf07069577","ku-13d9a170-9291-48a1-9988-d295445f092a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Resources and Evaluations for Danish Entity Resolution","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.21-038281","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Until recently, human behavioral data from reading has mainly been of interest to researchers to understand human cognition. However, these human language processing signals can also be beneficial in machine learning-based natural language processing tasks. Using EEG brain activity for this purpose is largely unexplored as of yet. In this paper, we present the first large-scale study of systematically analyzing the potential of EEG brain activity data for improving natural language processing tasks, with a special focus on which features of the signal are most beneficial. We present a multi-modal machine learning architecture that learns jointly from textual input as well as from EEG features. We find that filtering the EEG signals into frequency bands is more beneficial than using the broadband signal. Moreover, for a range of word embedding types, EEG data improves binary and ternary sentiment classification and outperforms multiple baselines. For more complex tasks such as relation detection, only the contextualized BERT embeddings outperform the baselines in our experiments, which raises the need for further research. Finally, EEG data shows to be particularly promising when limited training data is available.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hollenstein, Nora","Renggli, Cedric","Glaus, Benjamin","Barrett, Maria","Troendle, Marius","Langer, Nicolas","Zhang, Ce"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-038304"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","ETH Zürich","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zürich","University of Zurich"],"keyword":["Brain activity","EEG","Frequency bands","Machine learning","Multi modal learning","Natural Language Processing","Neural network","physiological data"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"decoding eeg brain activity for multi modal natural language processing","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fnhum.2021.659410","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-038304","identifier":[{"id":"85111356107","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8314009","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34326723","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["itu-55b2f51e-77c9-481c-a9e6-0d9fb6ff1dde","ku-ccbd4582-07d0-43e1-b597-13eee8532f23"],"keyword":["EEG","brain activity","frequency bands","machine learning","multi-modal learning","natural language processing","neural network","physiological data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-11326DAE28C97EC2435A315DEEBFF6AE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86398552/fnhum_15_659410.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fnhum.2021.659410/full","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fnhum.2021.659410","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/306969889/fnhum_15_659410.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Nordic Studies and Linguistics