Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-090.62-023335","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Eye-tracking data from reading provide a structured signal with a fine-grained temporal resolution which closely follows the sequential structure of the text. It is highly correlated with the cognitive load associated with different stages of human, cognitive text processing. While eye-tracking data have been extensively studied to understand human cognition, it has only recently been considered for Natural Language Processing (NLP). In this review, we provide a comprehensive overview of how gaze data are being used in data-driven NLP, in particular for sequence labelling and sequence classification tasks. We argue that eye-tracking may effectively counter one of the core challenges of machine-learning-based NLP: the scarcity of annotated data. We outline the recent advances in gaze-augmented NLP to discuss how the gaze signal from human readers can be leveraged while also considering the potentials and limitations of this data source.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Barrett, Maria Jung","Hollenstein, Nora"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-038377"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","ETH Zürich","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zürich"],"keyword":["Asymmetry","Eye tracking","Gaze","Human text processing","Movements","Natural Language Processing","Natural Reading","Sequence classification","Sequence labeling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sequence labelling and sequence classification with gaze novel uses of eye tracking data for natural language processing","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85544657/Accepted_version.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-038377","identifier":[{"id":"85091277451","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000571456700001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["itu-c1c37a5e-a0a0-4919-a1b9-f31c6f0d5ced","ku-ec9d384d-f5d7-494b-a642-17cb02977384"],"keyword":["ASYMMETRY","FIXATIONS","Human text processing","MOVEMENTS","Natural Reading","Sequence labeling","eye tracking","gaze","natural language processing","sequence classification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3429A3D46A72F5D91D86A23CB0DCCFCA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85544655/LangLinCompass_Submitted.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85544657/Accepted_version.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"eth zürich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"ETH Zürich","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal institute of technology zürich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zürich","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Maria","key":"barrettpau","last":"Barrett","locid":"45ecfb6f-78b7-405c-8bce-f8003b822bf9","name":"Barrett, Maria Jung","name_org":"Barrett, Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Nora","key":"hollensteinpau","last":"Hollenstein","name":"Hollenstein, Nora","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/lnc3.12396","issn":["1749818X"],"issue":"11","journal":"Language and Linguistics Compass","pages":"1-16","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Language and Linguistics Compass","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091277451"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c1c37a5e-a0a0-4919-a1b9-f31c6f0d5ced","ku-ec9d384d-f5d7-494b-a642-17cb02977384"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Sequence labelling and sequence classification with gaze : Novel uses of eye-tracking data for Natural Language Processing","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-038377","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Large-scale pretrained language models are the major driving force behind recent improvements in perfromance on the Winograd Schema Challenge, a widely employed test of commonsense reasoning ability. We show, however, with a new diagnostic dataset, that these models are sensitive to linguistic perturbations of the Winograd examples that minimally affect human understanding. Our results highlight interesting differences between humans and language models: language models are more sensitive to number or gender alternations and synonym replacements than humans, and humans are more stable and consistent in their predictions, maintain a much higher absolute performance, and perform better on non-associative instances than associative ones.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Abdou, Mostafa","Ravishankar, Vinit","Barrett, Maria Jung","Belinkov, Yonatan","Elliott, Desmond","Søgaard, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-532130"],"event":{"acronym":"ACL","end":"2020-07-10","place":"Online","start":"2020-07-05","title":"58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the sensitivity of language models and humans to winograd schema perturbations","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2020.acl-main.679","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-532130","identifier":[{"id":"85098815351","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e83f4751-0136-4024-8c6a-137b735d17a1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-04F15573225DA74F79DDB1AFEAA5313A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/258374822/The_Sensitivity_of_Language_Models_and_Humans.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2020.acl-main.679","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Machine Learning","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Natural Language Processing","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The Image Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mostafa","key":"abdoupau","last":"Abdou","locid":"6dd73bc7-0a10-4cc3-82da-59400ef3ec0d","name":"Abdou, Mostafa","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vinit","key":"ravishankarpau","last":"Ravishankar","name":"Ravishankar, Vinit","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria","key":"barrettpau","last":"Barrett","locid":"45ecfb6f-78b7-405c-8bce-f8003b822bf9","name":"Barrett, Maria Jung","name_org":"Barrett, Maria","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yonatan","key":"belinkovpau","last":"Belinkov","name":"Belinkov, Yonatan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Desmond","key":"elliottpau","last":"Elliott","locid":"8d2b3fbd-3993-4c1f-a661-fe1075081f31","name":"Elliott, Desmond","orcid":"0000-0003-3112-7904","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"5cfea506-104a-4b40-b63b-e29d037159b0","name":"Søgaard, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-5250-4276","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2020.acl-main.679","pages":"7590-7604","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e83f4751-0136-4024-8c6a-137b735d17a1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Sensitivity of Language Models and Humans to Winograd Schema Perturbations","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-532130","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The one-sided focus on English in previous studies of gender bias in NLP misses out on opportunities in other languages: English challenge datasets such as GAP and WinoGender highlight model preferences that are “hallucinatory”, e.g., disambiguating gender-ambiguous occurrences of ‘doctor’ as male doctors. We show that for languages with type B reflexivization, e.g., Swedish and Russian, we can construct multi-task challenge datasets for detecting gender bias that lead to unambiguously wrong model predictions: In these languages, the direct translation of ‘the doctor removed his mask’ is not ambiguous between a coreferential reading and a disjoint reading. Instead, the coreferential reading requires a non-gendered pronoun, and the gendered, possessive pronouns are anti-reflexive. We present a multilingual, multi-task challenge dataset, which spans four languages and four NLP tasks and focuses only on this phenomenon. We find evidence for gender bias across all task-language combinations and correlate model bias with national labor market statistics.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Gonzalez, Ana Valeria","Barrett, Maria Jung","Hvingelby, Rasmus","Søgaard, Anders","Webster, Kellie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-438418"],"event":{"acronym":"EMNLP","end":"2020-11-20","place":"online","start":"2020-11-16","title":"The 2020 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Google"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-ALX"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-ALX","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"type b reflexivization as an unambiguous testbed for multilingual multi task gender bias","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2020.emnlp-main.209","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-438418","ids":["ku-4b6da67a-773d-4509-9e83-2029db8f6f56"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-30ECD556DEB39EA4A440BEB21F0FF071"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2020.emnlp-main.209","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/258399672/Type_B_Reflexivization_as_an_Unambiguous_Testbed.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Machine Learning","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Natural Language Processing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"alexandra institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-ALX","l3nn":"Alexandra Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Alexandra Institute","namevar":["Alexandra Instituttet A/S (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-ALX","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"google","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Google","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ana Valeria","key":"gonzalezpau","last":"Gonzalez","locid":"15bca55a-7863-4892-ae02-56f2d27225e7","name":"Gonzalez, Ana Valeria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Maria Jung","key":"barrettpau","last":"Barrett","locid":"45ecfb6f-78b7-405c-8bce-f8003b822bf9","name":"Barrett, Maria Jung","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rasmus","key":"hvingelbypau","last":"Hvingelby","name":"Hvingelby, Rasmus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"5cfea506-104a-4b40-b63b-e29d037159b0","name":"Søgaard, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-5250-4276","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Kellie","key":"websterpau","last":"Webster","name":"Webster, Kellie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2020.emnlp-main.209","pages":"2637-2648","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2020 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4b6da67a-773d-4509-9e83-2029db8f6f56"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Type B Reflexivization as an Unambiguous Testbed for Multilingual Multi-Task Gender Bias","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-438418","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Hollenstein, Nora","Barrett, Maria Jung","Beinborn, Lisa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-413737"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards best practices for leveraging human language processing signals for natural language processing","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2020.lincr-1.3/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-413737","ids":["ku-21f44400-73fd-4323-8524-ffb54388d2a8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9E7CD2DBA2506898641C6D34A0E48820"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2020.lincr-1.3/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Nordic Studies and Linguistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"vrije universiteit amsterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nora","key":"hollensteinpau","last":"Hollenstein","locid":"2a55bbfd-d9e9-448c-a4fd-baddb8ce0714","name":"Hollenstein, Nora","orcid":"0000-0001-7936-4170","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria Jung","key":"barrettpau","last":"Barrett","locid":"45ecfb6f-78b7-405c-8bce-f8003b822bf9","name":"Barrett, Maria Jung","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lisa","key":"beinbornpau","last":"Beinborn","name":"Beinborn, Lisa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"15-27","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Second Workshop on Linguistic and Neurocognitive Resources"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-21f44400-73fd-4323-8524-ffb54388d2a8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards Best Practices for Leveraging Human Language Processing Signals for Natural Language Processing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-413737","year":"2020","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Kunstig intelligens står for stort set alle nye landvindinger inden for sprogteknologi. Udviklingen går så hurtigt, at den enkelte underviser selv skal kunne vurdere relevansen af nye teknologier. Kunstig intelligens kan effektivisere nuværende læse- og skriveteknologier og synliggøre nye sider af læringsprocessen, men der er ikke noget i teknologierne, der ændrer på det faktum, at eleverne skal øve sig på at læse og skrive","author_count":2,"contributors":["Klerke, Sigrid","Barrett, Maria Jung"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-481880"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hvordan kunstig intelligens bliver til læse og skriveteknologier","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.videnomlaesning.dk/media/2947/26_sigrid-klerke_maria-barrett-1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-481880","ids":["ku-9406c48c-36d7-47b8-9734-168614ae4920"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-718EE32F4A22E7EA4481F1F422FD3DE9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.videnomlaesning.dk/media/2947/26_sigrid-klerke_maria-barrett-1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Sigrid","key":"klerkepau","last":"Klerke","name":"Klerke, Sigrid","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria Jung","key":"barrettpau","last":"Barrett","locid":"45ecfb6f-78b7-405c-8bce-f8003b822bf9","name":"Barrett, Maria Jung","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["22452761","22466525"],"issn_org":["22466517"],"issue":"26","journal":"Viden om Literacy","pages":"32-37","status":"p","title":"Viden om Literacy","volume":"2019"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9406c48c-36d7-47b8-9734-168614ae4920"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hvordan kunstig intelligens bliver til læse og skriveteknologier","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-481880","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Elazar and Goldberg (2018) showed that protected attributes can be extracted from the representations of a debiased neural network for mention detection at above-chance levels, by evaluating a diagnostic classifier on a held-out subsample of the data it was trained on. We revisit their experiments and conduct a series of follow-up experiments showing that, in fact, the diagnostic classifier generalizes poorly to both new in-domain samples and new domains, indicating that it relies on correlations specific to their particular data sample. We further show that a diagnostic classifier trained on the biased baseline neural network also does not generalize to new samples. In other words, the biases detected in Elazar and Goldberg (2018) seem restricted to their particular data sample, and would therefore not bias the decisions of the model on new samples, whether in-domain or out-of-domain. In light of this, we discuss better methodologies for detecting bias in our models.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Barrett, Maria Jung","Kementchedjhieva, Yova Radoslavova","Elazar, Yanai","Elliott, Desmond","Søgaard, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-449031"],"event":{"acronym":"IJCNPL","end":"2019-11-07","place":"Hong Kong, cn","start":"2019-11-03","title":"2019 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing and the 9th International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing (EMNLP-IJCNLP)","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adversarial removal of demographic attributes revisited","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/D19-1662","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-449031","identifier":[{"id":"85084294832","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5cdb0c5b-d118-40d1-a526-082e35129172"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-EB4829FC599144A49157798BBCB8F1D0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/D19-1662","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Maria","key":"barrettpau","last":"Barrett","locid":"45ecfb6f-78b7-405c-8bce-f8003b822bf9","name":"Barrett, Maria Jung","name_org":"Barrett, Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yova","key":"kementchedjhievapau","last":"Kementchedjhieva","locid":"7034649e-ee67-43a1-a49e-134d9c7ee897","name":"Kementchedjhieva, Yova Radoslavova","name_org":"Kementchedjhieva, Yova","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yanai","key":"elazarpau","last":"Elazar","name":"Elazar, Yanai","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Desmond","key":"elliottpau","last":"Elliott","locid":"8d2b3fbd-3993-4c1f-a661-fe1075081f31","name":"Elliott, Desmond","orcid":"0000-0003-3112-7904","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"5cfea506-104a-4b40-b63b-e29d037159b0","name":"Søgaard, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-5250-4276","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/d19-1662","pages":"6329-6334","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2019 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing and the 9th International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing (EMNLP-IJCNLP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084294832"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5cdb0c5b-d118-40d1-a526-082e35129172"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Adversarial Removal of Demographic Attributes Revisited","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-449031","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"When humans perform everyday tasks like reading, speaking, and writing, they cognitively also completemany of the tasks that natural language processing strives for computers to replicate. The traces of humancognitive processing can be collected in various data sources such as eye tracking during reading, keystrokelogs from typing and acoustic cues, where milliseconds matter.This thesis shows that there is an unused potential for utilizing eye tracking and other data sourcesreflecting human cognitive processing of text for natural language processing.This thesis presents several studies where traces of human text processing can be used to improve a broadrange of established natural language processing tasks. The tasks span part-of-speech induction, syntacticparsing, sentiment classification, grammatical error detection and detection of abusive language. The thesisfurthermore demonstrates some transfer across related languages by using English eye-tracking recordingsto improve French part-of-speech induction.Technology for recording keystroke logs and prosody features is already common. And the recentadvancements of low-cost eye tracking technology promise eye-tracking data to be available in largerquantities, also for low-resource languages. Real-world eye-tracking data poses new challenges comparedto laboratory data. One study in this thesis presents first evidence that despite the noise and idiosyncrasies,real-world reading data recorded with a consumer-grade eye tracker can be modelled in machine learningmodels.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Barrett, Maria Jung"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-522222"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improving natural language processing with human data eye tracking and other data sources reflecting cognitive text processing","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-522222","ids":["ku-d7912525-4c39-49b4-9aad-66a84b899371"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5F9FE4D4A4BC1F4A84BD7E10DCE23341"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Nordic Studies and Linguistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Maria","key":"barrettpau","last":"Barrett","locid":"45ecfb6f-78b7-405c-8bce-f8003b822bf9","name":"Barrett, Maria Jung","name_org":"Barrett, Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"171","publisher":"Det Humanistiske Fakultet, Københavns Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d7912525-4c39-49b4-9aad-66a84b899371"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Improving natural language processing with human data : Eye tracking and other data sources reflecting cognitive text processing","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-522222","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"When learning POS taggers and syntactic chunkers for low-resource languages, different resources may be available, and often all we have is a small tag dictionary, motivating type-constrained unsupervised induction. Even small dictionaries can improve the performance of unsupervised induction algorithms. This paper shows that performance can be further improved by including data that is readily available or can be easily obtained for most languages, i.e., eye-tracking, speech, or keystroke logs (or any combination thereof). We project information from all these data sources into shared spaces, in which the union of words is represented. For English unsupervised POS induction, the additional information, which is not required at test time, leads to an average error reduction on Ontonotes domains of 1.5% over systems augmented with state-of-the-art word embeddings. On Penn Treebank the best model achieves 5.4% error reduction over a word embeddings baseline. We also achieve significant improvements for syntactic chunk induction. Our analysis shows that improvements are even bigger when the available tag dictionaries are smaller.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Barrett, Maria Jung","Gonzalez, Ana Valeria","Frermann, Lea","Søgaard, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-421678"],"event":{"acronym":"NAACL HLT","end":"2018-06-06","place":"New Orleans, us","start":"2018-06-01","title":"16th Annual Conference of the North American Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Human Language Technologies","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Amazon Development Center"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unsupervised induction of linguistic categories with records of reading speaking and writing","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.aclweb.org/anthology/N18-1184","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-421678","identifier":[{"id":"85083528377","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-2f629969-d6ca-4f4d-ada2-1de93ed6b658"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-3-BD886C6FA3DAEAE9ADB16219F3AC348F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Nordic Studies and Linguistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Amazon Development Center"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Maria Jung","key":"barrettpau","last":"Barrett","locid":"45ecfb6f-78b7-405c-8bce-f8003b822bf9","name":"Barrett, Maria Jung","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ana Valeria","key":"gonzalezpau","last":"Gonzalez","locid":"15bca55a-7863-4892-ae02-56f2d27225e7","name":"Gonzalez, Ana Valeria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lea","key":"frermannpau","last":"Frermann","name":"Frermann, Lea","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"5cfea506-104a-4b40-b63b-e29d037159b0","name":"Søgaard, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-5250-4276","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Silvio Ricardo","key":"cordeiropedh","last":"Cordeiro","name":"Cordeiro, Silvio Ricardo","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Shereen","key":"orabypedh","last":"Oraby","name":"Oraby, Shereen","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Umashanthi","key":"pavalanathanpedh","last":"Pavalanathan","name":"Pavalanathan, Umashanthi","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kyeongmin","key":"rimpedh","last":"Rim","name":"Rim, Kyeongmin","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/n18-1184","isbn":["9781948087278"],"pages":"2028-2038","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","subtitle":"Human Language Technologies, (Long Papers)","title":"Proceedings of the 2018 Conference of the North American Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics (NAACL)","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083528377"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2f629969-d6ca-4f4d-ada2-1de93ed6b658"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Unsupervised Induction of Linguistic Categories with Records of Reading, Speaking, and Writing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-421678","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Barrett, Maria Jung","Bingel, Joachim","Klerke, Sigrid","Balling, Laura Winther"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-514868"],"event":{"end":"2018-08-24","place":"Frederiksberg, dk","start":"2018-08-23","title":"Scandinavian Workshop on Applied Eye Tracking - SWAET 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using naturalistic eye tracking data to understand children s reading difficulties poster abstract","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://bop.unibe.ch/JEMR/article/view/SWAET2018-Abstracts/SWAET2018_Abstracts","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-514868","ids":["ku-cb5b610d-1368-4219-92bf-a0ea4c894209"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A9A24124F845F50B0C4EEEE5C9FEDC8C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://bop.unibe.ch/JEMR/article/view/SWAET2018-Abstracts/SWAET2018_Abstracts","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["EyeJustRead Denmark ApS (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Maria Jung","key":"barrettpau","last":"Barrett","locid":"45ecfb6f-78b7-405c-8bce-f8003b822bf9","name":"Barrett, Maria Jung","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Joachim","key":"bingelpau","last":"Bingel","locid":"0ddc044d-124c-4c51-a305-4a61d6e1ea9f","name":"Bingel, Joachim","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sigrid","key":"klerkepau","last":"Klerke","name":"Klerke, Sigrid","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Laura Winther","key":"ballingpau","last":"Balling","name":"Balling, Laura Winther","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19958692"],"issue":"5","journal":"Journal of Eye Movement Research","pages":"32","status":"p","title":"Journal of Eye Movement Research","volume":"11"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","eyejustread denmark aps (biz)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cb5b610d-1368-4219-92bf-a0ea4c894209"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Using naturalistic eye‐tracking data to understand children’s reading difficulties[Poster/Abstract}","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-514868","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Learning attention functions requires large volumes of data, but many NLP tasks simulate human behavior, and in this paper, we show that human attention really does provide a good inductive bias on many attention functions in NLP. Specifically, we use estimated human attention derived from eyetracking corpora to regularize attention functions in recurrent neural networks. We show substantial improvements across a range of tasks, including sentiment analysis, grammatical error detection, and detection of abusive language.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Barrett, Maria Jung","Bingel, Joachim","Hollenstein, Nora","Rei, Marek","Søgaard, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-541238"],"event":{"end":"2018-11-01","place":"Brussels, be","start":"2018-10-31","title":"22nd Conference on Computational Natural Language Learning (CoNLL 2018)","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sequence classification with human attention","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/231308570/Best_paper_award.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-541238","ids":["ku-f78fb48e-e4a0-4cec-9bf7-355e0e958cfb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B8C79865B090C9936768F22D7B0344A1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/231308570/Best_paper_award.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Nordic Studies and Linguistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Maria Jung","key":"barrettpau","last":"Barrett","locid":"45ecfb6f-78b7-405c-8bce-f8003b822bf9","name":"Barrett, Maria Jung","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Joachim","key":"bingelpau","last":"Bingel","locid":"0ddc044d-124c-4c51-a305-4a61d6e1ea9f","name":"Bingel, Joachim","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nora","key":"hollensteinpau","last":"Hollenstein","locid":"2a55bbfd-d9e9-448c-a4fd-baddb8ce0714","name":"Hollenstein, Nora","orcid":"0000-0001-7936-4170","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marek","key":"reipau","last":"Rei","name":"Rei, Marek","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"5cfea506-104a-4b40-b63b-e29d037159b0","name":"Søgaard, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-5250-4276","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna","key":"korhonenpedh","last":"Korhonen","name":"Korhonen, Anna","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ivan","key":"titovpedh","last":"Titov","name":"Titov, Ivan","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781948087728"],"pages":"302-312","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 22nd Conference on Computational Natural Language Learning (CoNLL 2018)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85072108267"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f78fb48e-e4a0-4cec-9bf7-355e0e958cfb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Sequence classification with human attention","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-541238","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"We present the first work on predicting reading mistakes in children with reading difficulties based on eye-tracking data from real-world reading teaching. Our approach employs sev-eral linguistic and gaze-based features to in-form an ensemble of different classifiers, in-cluding multi-task learning models that let us transfer knowledge about individual readers to attain better predictions. Notably, the data we use in this work stems from noisy readings in the wild, outside of controlled lab condi-tions. Our experiments show that despite the noise and despite the small fraction of mis-readings, gaze data improves the performance more than any other feature group and our models achieve good performance. We further show that gaze patterns for misread words do not fully generalize across readers, but that we can transfer some knowledge between readers using multitask learning at least in some cases. Applications of our models include partial au-tomation of reading assessment as well as per-sonalized text simplification.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bingel, Joachim","Barrett, Maria Jung","Klerke, Sigrid"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-498891"],"event":{"end":"2018-06-05","place":"New Orleans, us","start":"2018-06-05","title":"13h Workshop on Innovative Use of NLP for Building Educational Applications","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"predicting misreadings from gaze in children with reading difficulties","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.mendeley.com/research/predicting-misreadings-gaze-children-reading-difficulties","